    <innernamespace refid="namespaceOpenSkyhawk">OpenSkyhawk</innernamespace>
    <briefdescription>
<para>The Gateway uploader&apos;s USB contract (#366) — states, phases, results and payload layouts of the UPL_* messages. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The messages ride the calibration channel&apos;s envelope (<computeroutput>AA 53 4B 43</computeroutput>, TYPE, SEQ, LEN-exact, CRC16); their type codes and NACK reasons are in <ref refid="AxisCal_8h" kindref="compound">AxisCal.h</ref> (<computeroutput>CAL_T_UPL_*</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>CAL_NACK_BUSY</computeroutput>…). The client streams an image, the Gateway stages and verifies it, then flashes a board&apos;s bootloader over CAN through <ref refid="namespacePanelBridge" kindref="compound">PanelBridge</ref> — and finishes on its own if the client goes away. Behaviour: FirmwarePlan/07-simgateway-api.md § <ref refid="namespaceUploader" kindref="compound">Uploader</ref>; messages: FirmwarePlan/03-uart-usb-hid-protocol.md.</para>
<para>Every value is a named enum or constexpr so the client sync can read it (#346).</para>
<para><simplesect kind="copyright"><para>GPL-2.0-only — see Firmware/LICENSE </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
